],["לְהַעֲבִיד","leha'avid","H5647","HR/Vhcc","to compel to labor"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הָעָם","ha'am","H5971","HTd/Ncmsa","the people"]],"x":[[14002002,14002002,3]],"xn":1}},"people":[{"id":"solomon_2762","name":"Solomon","also":"Jedidiah","summary":"Peaceful, (Heb. Shelomoh), David’s second son by Bathsheba, i.e., the first after their legal marriage (2 Sam. 12). He was probably born about B.C. 1035 (1 Chr. 22:5; 29:1).","verses":273,"father":"David","mother":"Bathsheba","v":[1,2,3,11,17]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[3,7,12,14,17]},{"id":"hiram_1532","name":"Hiram","also":"Huram","summary":"Also “Huram” and “Horam,” king of Tyre. He entered into an alliance with David, and assisted him in building his palace by sending him able workmen, and also cedar-trees and fir-trees from Lebanon (2 Sam. 5:11; 1 Chr. 14:1).","verses":23,"father":"Huram","mother":"","v":[3,11,12]},{"id":"huram_1575","name":"Huram","also":"","summary":"A man of great skill.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[14]}],"places":[{"id":"tyre_1184","name":"Tyre","kind":"City","lat":33.26807,"lon":35.20936,"summary":"A rock, now es-Sur; an ancient Phoenician city, about 23 miles, in a direct line, north of Acre, and 20 south of Sidon. Sidon was the oldest Phoenician city, but Tyre had a longer and more illustrious history.","verses":52,"v":[3,11,14]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[7,16]},{"id":"lebanon_720","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":33.92154,"lon":35.89897,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":56,"v":[8,16]},{"id":"joppa_652","name":"Joppa","kind":"City","lat":32.05372,"lon":34.75212,"summary":"Beauty, a town in the portion of Dan (Josh. 19:46; A.V., “Japho”), on a sandy promontory between Caesarea and Gaza, and at a distance of 30 miles north-west from Jerusalem.","verses":14,"v":[16]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[8010,8010,559,1129,1129,1004,1004,8034,8034,8034,3068,3068,3068,4438,4438,4438,1004,1004,1004],[5608,5608,5608,7657,5449,8084,2672,2022,2022,2022,7969,7969,5329],[8010,8010,7971,413,413,2361,4428,6865,6865,834,834,834,834,6213,6213,5973,1,1,1732,7971,7971,7971,0,730,1129,1129,0,1004,1004,3427,3427,0],[2009,1129,1129,1129,1129,1129,1004,1004,8034,8034,8034,3068,3068,3068,430,430,6942,6942,0,0,6999,6999,5561,7004,6440,6440,4635,4635,4635,4635,8548,5930,5930,5930,5930,5930,1242,1242,6153,6153,7676,7676,7676,7676,7676,7676,2320,2320,4150,4150,4150,3068,3068,3068,430,430,2063,5921,5921,5921,3478,3478],[1004,1004,834,589,1129,1129,1419,1419,1419,3588,430,430,1419,1419,3605,3605,430],[4310,4310,6113,6113,1129,1129,1004,1004,0,0,3588,8064,8064,8064,8064,8064,8064,3808,3557,3557,4310,4310,589,589,834,1129,1129,1129,1004,1004,0,0,3588,3588,3588,3588,6999,6999,6999,6440,6440],[7971,0,6258,376,376,3045,6605,6605,6213,6213,2091,2091,3701,3701,5178,5178,1270,1270,710,710,710,3758,8504,8504,8504,5973,5973,5973,5973,2450,2450,3063,3063,3389,3389,834,1,1,1732,3559],[7971,7971,0,730,1265,418,418,6086,3844,3844,3588,589,3045,834,5650,5650,3045,3045,3772,37